
  Tests (3)
    ✖ skip-added             error    New skip/disable markers (`it.skip`, `xit`,
                                      `@pytest.mark.skip`, `t.Skip`, `#[ignore]`, `@Disabled`).
    ✖ focus-added            error    `.only`, `fit`, `fdescribe`: silently skips every other test
                                      in the file.
    ▲ assertion-weakened     warning  A specific matcher was replaced by a weaker one (`toEqual(x)`
                                      → `toBeDefined()`), or a tolerance was widened.

  Accounting (2)
    ✖ assertions-removed     error    A surviving test lost assertions (`3 → 1`).
    ▲ test-file-deleted      warning  A test file was deleted and its tests were not re-added
                                      elsewhere.

  Escapes (3)
    ▲ any-cast               warning  `as any`, `as unknown as T`, `<any>`, `cast(Any, ...)` (info
                                      in tests).
    ▲ lint-suppressed        warning  `eslint-disable`, `# noqa`, `//nolint`, `#[allow(...)]`,
                                      `@SuppressWarnings` (info in tests).
    ▲ hardcoded-answer       warning  Source special-cases a literal that the tests use as input or
                                      expected output.

  CI (2)
    ✖ ci-failure-ignored     error    `continue-on-error: true`, `allow_failure: true`, `|| true` on
                                      a verification command.
    ✖ coverage-lowered       error    Coverage thresholds were lowered or removed.

  Integrity (2)
    ✖ protected-path         error    A file matching a `protected:` glob in .narc.yml was modified
                                      or deleted.
    ▲ waiver-missing-reason  warning  A narc:allow comment must say why the waived change is
                                      acceptable.

  12 rules · narc explain <rule> for details

